An identity conversion whose source is written as an explicit conversion keeps the
type-naming diagnostic: the user really did spell both sides, so "source and target are
both MyInt" is accurate here, unlike the bare-constant form, which gets its own message.
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
error-is: ErrInvalidConversion
-- example.com/app/a.go --
package app

type MyInt int

//plumb:build
var _ MyInt = MyInt(5)
